      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ostial intracoronary stent deployment is complicated by the influence of cardiac motion, which causes the stent to oscillate back and forth during the cardiac cycle. Accurate deployment can be facilitated by initial low pressure inflation of the balloon on which the stent is mounted. This stabilizes the stent within the stenosis, while still allowing adjustment of the exact stent location prior to deployment."},
